; Newsdesk burned-in subtitle style — paper-diorama kit
;
; Bold condensed sans, uppercase, paper-cream ink on a hard black outline.
;
; INVERTED FROM THE HOUSE FILE, and for the same reason the house file gives.
; The house ground is warm cream paper, so its captions are ink-dark inside a
; pale pasteboard halo. This ground is aged sepia newsprint under tungsten light
; with deep shadows, and dark type on it disappears into the shadow side of every
; frame. So the fill is paper cream and the outline is press black — a caption
; struck onto the sheet rather than one printed into it.
;
; SAME FACE AS THE HOUSE, deliberately. Anton IS a bold condensed sans, it is the
; typeface the app's own stamps use, and it is the one face already verified as
; resolvable on the machine that burns. A second family here would buy a marginal
; difference in flavour and pay for it with the exact failure the house file
; warns about: ffmpeg does not embed fonts, and a missing face falls back
; SILENTLY to something else that nobody notices until the render is watched.
; If this kit ever gets its own face, install it first and verify it the same way.
;
; Colours are tokens, not inventions, and each one is a real element of the style:
;   paper cream   #EDE4D3  ->  &H00D3E4ED   the newsprint sheet itself
;   press black   #14110D  ->  &H000D1114   the censor bar
;   burnt orange  #C6541F  ->  &H001F54C6   the single accent, and the ONLY place
;                                           a second colour is allowed on screen
; ASS stores colour as &HAABBGGRR — bytes reversed from hex RGB, alpha 00 = opaque.
;
; The Number style carries the accent for the same reason the through-line object
; does: in this world one colour means "look here", and spending it on anything
; but the figure that matters spends the frame's only emphasis on nothing.
;
; PlayRes is the 9:16 delivery frame — 1080x1920, matching the house file, NOT the
; reference style's 16:9. See scene-guidance.txt for why the aspect deviates and
; why it must not be "fixed" back. libass scales outline and shadow with PlayRes
; (ScaledBorderAndShadow: yes), so burning at another output size keeps these
; proportions rather than producing hairline outlines.
;
; The outline is one point heavier than the house file (8 against 7) because
; tungsten light on newsprint puts more mid-tone directly behind the type than a
; flat cream ground does.
;
; PREREQUISITE FOR ASSEMBLY: Anton must be resolvable by libass on the machine
; running the burn.  Verify with:  fc-list | grep -i anton

